<Mod>
	<Name>Node Editor</Name>
	<Author>wizz6rd</Author>
	<Version>0.1.0</Version>

	<Description>
	Two blocks, each of which is up to thirty-two of Besiege's own.

	Timer Plus is up to thirty-two of Besiege's timer blocks. Each row of its
	table is a timer with the same settings the game's own has -- activation key
	or variable, hold to run, allow stop, loop, wait, emulation duration and the
	key or variable it presses -- and the rows can be sorted by any column. A
	button at the bottom converts the table into that many real timer blocks,
	laid out on one horizontal plane and handed over as a selection.

	Node Editor is the same table for Besiege's logic gates: two inputs, the
	gate, its one switch and the key it presses, a row apiece -- and a board to
	wire those rows on as nodes, timers among them.

	Block models by Poly by Google and Robert Schlyter, from Poly Pizza, under
	CC-BY 3.0. The settings
	panel needs UI Factory (Workshop item 2913469777); without it the block falls
	back to Besiege's own block mapper.
	</Description>

	<!-- The node editor's own hotkeys. Declared here so Besiege puts them in its
	     controls screen and the player can rebind them like any other.

	     The modifier is the 1 key rather than Control on purpose: Besiege's own
	     copy and paste are Ctrl+C and Ctrl+V, the game gets the keyboard at the
	     same time this does, and a board paste that also duplicated the block
	     under it is not a paste anybody asked for. -->
	<Keys>
		<Key name="board-copy" defaultModifier="Alpha1" defaultTrigger="C" />
		<Key name="board-paste" defaultModifier="Alpha1" defaultTrigger="V" />
		<Key name="board-select-all" defaultModifier="Alpha1" defaultTrigger="A" />
	</Keys>

	<Icon name="NodeEditor_icon" />
	<Debug>false</Debug>
	<MultiplayerCompatible>true</MultiplayerCompatible>

	<Assemblies>
		<Assembly path="NodeEditor.dll" />
	</Assemblies>

	<Blocks>
		<Block path="TimerPlus.xml" />
		<Block path="NodeEditor.xml" />
	</Blocks>

	<Resources>
		<Mesh name="TimerPlus_mesh" path="TimerPlus.obj" />
		<Texture name="TimerPlus_texture" path="TimerPlus.png" />
		<Mesh name="NodeEditor_mesh" path="NodeEditor.obj" />
		<Texture name="NodeEditor_texture" path="NodeEditor.png" />
		<Texture name="NodeEditor_icon" path="Thumbnail.png" />

		<!-- The table's three switch columns are headed with a picture rather
		     than a letter. Drawn by tools/make-ui-icons.py from the artwork in
		     tools/icons; loaded by name in Glyphs.cs. -->
		<Texture name="NodeEditor_hold" path="Hold.png" />
		<Texture name="NodeEditor_stop" path="Stop.png" />
		<Texture name="NodeEditor_loop" path="Loop.png" />

		<!-- The node editor's own two: the comment node's picture in its palette,
